      </infoLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="02dc-e73d-f9f7-357a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Mercenaries" id="17cb-dfc2-d32b-4121" hidden="false">
          <description>The leadership of the Kroot is not fixed, instead is considered equal to their points value. Normally it is 7, but if they are upgraded with a 6+ Armor save it increeases to 8. Note that the presence of a Kroot Shaper, Kroot Hounds or a Krootox doesn&apos;t directly affect the Leadership of the squad.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Eaters of the Dead" id="ded2-3151-7ce0-dbc5" hidden="false">
          <description>Kroot must pass a Leadership test in order to pursue a foe defeated in close combat or make a sweeping advance. If the test is failed the Kroot must instead consolidate. If a Kroot Shaper is in the squad then they MUST consolidate, they have no choice.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Fieldcraft" id="91cd-ebc7-b892-3f86" hidden="false">
          <description>Kroot gain +1 to their cover save in woods or jungles. Kroot in woods or jungles do not roll a Difficult Terrain test; they may always move up to 6&quot;. If they do not move in the movement phase they may see and shoot through 12&quot; of woods or jungle terrain rather than the normal 6&quot;</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
